# SHA-256 of each normalised red-list term (lowercase, punctuation
# stripped, whitespace collapsed) — never the term itself. Populate via:
#   node scripts/disclosure-check.mjs --add
# (reads one term from stdin, hashes it, appends here, never echoes it)
#
# Empty as of Phase 0: the architecture component names, layer configs,
# specific diagnostic findings and the ablation table are red-list-dense
# material this build was explicitly told not to read (brief's Reference
# table, `Desktop/Seizure EEG` row). The regex category layer in
# scripts/disclosure-check.mjs already covers the public *shapes* of
# banned information (AUROC, event-F1, ablation, sensitivity=N, CGPA,
# phone-number shapes) without needing the terms themselves. This file
# is where the author adds the specific vocabulary via --add before
# Phase 12 sign-off.
#
# Phase 0 proof: a synthetic term was added via --add, injected into
# index.html, confirmed the checker failed and named the file:line without
# ever printing the term, then both the injection and the hash were
# reverted. The mechanism works.
